<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="54980" href="schedule/2011/spring/GWS/395/54980.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120111" href="schedule/2011/spring.xml">Spring 2011</term><subject id="GWS" href="schedule/2011/spring/GWS.xml">Gender and Women's Studies</subject><course id="395" href="schedule/2011/spring/GWS/395.xml">Intermediate Topics GWS</course></parents><sectionNumber>TB </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Writing Lives This course will explore autobiography in the contemporary world. We will explore theories of autobiography, ask how writing about the self is gendered, and how representations of the self fare in the outside world. The course will examine how changing media such as film, television and cyberspace affect these representations. We will also discuss issues how theories of autobiography fare when applied to cross-cultural writings.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-01-18Z</startDate><endDate>2011-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G30</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Barnes" firstName="T">Barnes, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>